WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.480
Would "The Princess Bride" make a perfect double&nbsp;
feature with "The Mummy?" What do Robin Williams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.880
and Brendan Fraser have in common? These are the&nbsp;
adventure films to watch if you love "The Mummy."

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.080
Fans looking to get their adventure fix need&nbsp;
look no further than Dr. Henry "Indiana" Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.400
as played by legendary actor Harrison Ford;&nbsp;
he's been rocking the whip and fedora combo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.040
for the last 30 years! To date, his tenure&nbsp;
as the archaeologist-slash-adventurer has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.720
resulted in four films, with a fifth&nbsp;
"Indiana Jones" film in the works.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.720
It all kicked off with 1981's "Raiders of&nbsp;
the Lost Ark," in which Indy searches for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.320
the fabled Ark of the Covenant — believed&nbsp;
to contain the stone tablets on which the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.080
Ten Commandments were inscribed — which is&nbsp;
supposed to have the power to make one's army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.080
undefeatable. Who would be interested&nbsp;
in such an ability? Nazis, that's who;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.480
the fascist German regime would appear again&nbsp;
as adversaries in 1989's third installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.640
"Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade,"&nbsp;
which included a quest for the Holy Grail.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.920
The second film, 1984's "Indiana&nbsp;
Jones and the Temple of Doom,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.280
served as a prequel to "Raiders"&nbsp;
and was primarily set in India,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.040
with Dr. Jones taking on a Thuggee&nbsp;
cult and its chief priest, Mola Ram.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.480
"Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal&nbsp;
Skull" came out in 2008 and swaps the Soviet Union&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.840
and its KGB in as Indy's antagonists. It has the&nbsp;
distinction of faring the worst with reviewers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.880
though its 78% critics score and Certified Fresh&nbsp;
distinction on Rotten Tomatoes simply reflect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.600
how beloved the franchise is as a whole.&nbsp;
By any name, "Indiana Jones" is a classic.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.520
"I like Indiana."

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.840
"We named the dog Indiana."

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:30.320
"Sahara" is a fun 2005 action-adventure&nbsp;
flick starring Matthew McConaughey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.400
as late author Clive Cussler's prolific&nbsp;
adventurer Dirk Pitt, adapted from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.800
novel of the same name. In "Sahara," Pitt is&nbsp;
searching for some long lost treasure: the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:44.000
haul of gold that was loaded onto the Confederate&nbsp;
ship CSS Texas at the end of the U.S. Civil War.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.640
Despite its talented cast and intriguing&nbsp;
plot, "Sahara" was mostly panned by critics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.373
managing just a meager 38%&nbsp;
critics score on Rotten Tomatoes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.760
Viewers were a bit kinder to the film, though,&nbsp;
as evidenced by its 53% audience score. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.840
addition to its lack of critical success,&nbsp;
the film was beset by numerous problems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:07.440
including a massive $160 million budget that was&nbsp;
doubled from its original $80 million. According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.640
to “The Los Angeles Times,” "Sahara" is believed&nbsp;
to have lost the studio $78 million, making it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.760
among the biggest box office bombs of all time.&nbsp;
But it's still a fun popcorn movie for date night!

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.560
Looking for Indiana Jones, but with a&nbsp;
little less swagger and a much bigger brain?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.200
Meet Noah Wyle as Flynn Carsen, the title&nbsp;
character of the "Librarian" franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.920
Think of "The Librarian" as the&nbsp;
ultimate keeper of knowledge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.040
in addition to being the protector&nbsp;
of the actual Tree of Knowledge.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.400
Over the course of three films — including 2006's&nbsp;
"The Librarian: Return to King Solomon's Mines,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.040
and 2008's "The Librarian: Curse of the Judas&nbsp;
Chalice" — the totally bookish and mostly meek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.440
hero tracks down the Spear of Destiny, searches&nbsp;
for ancient treasure, and meets the girl of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.440
dreams while trying to protect the vampire&nbsp;
equivalent of the Holy Grail. That's in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:56.657
addition to inspiring the spinoff TV series "The&nbsp;
Librarians," which ran for four seasons on TNT.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.360
You can't compile a list of adventure movies&nbsp;
worth watching without including the "National&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.800
Treasure" franchise. The 2004 film and its 2007&nbsp;
sequel, "National Treasure: Book of Secrets,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.080
feature actor and human meme Nicolas Cage, as&nbsp;
historian and adventurer Benjamin Franklin Gates.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.280
The first installment sees him steal&nbsp;
the Declaration of Independence from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.200
the National Archives in Washington, D.C.,&nbsp;
but don't worry, it's totally for a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.040
cause — protecting it from other thieves&nbsp;
led by a former friend and colleague.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.040
All parties concerned are in search of a storied&nbsp;
treasure trove from the Founding Fathers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.280
believe the Declaration contains a clue that'll&nbsp;
put them closer to their goals of finding it.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.360
The sequel sees Gates setting about defending&nbsp;
the honor of his ancestor Thomas Gates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.520
who was tasked with decrypting John Wilkes&nbsp;
Booth's journal; he did so and failed to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:44.240
the assassination of Abraham Lincoln, ultimately&nbsp;
dying at the hand of Confederate sympathizers.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.840
Though it's been a decade and a half since&nbsp;
the last film, fans have reason to be excited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.001
as Disney has announced both a third&nbsp;
film and a new TV series on Disney+.

00:03:52.897 --> 00:03:56.800
The "Mummy" franchise was so successful, it&nbsp;
spawned a spinoff film series tied to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.440
second movie. "The Mummy Returns" sees our hero&nbsp;
trying to save his son, who's foolishly put on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.000
Bracelet of Anubis and will die if they don't&nbsp;
get him to a magical locale in a week's time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.440
There, Rick O'Connell does battle with&nbsp;
the equally mythical Scorpion King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.840
who sold his soul to Anubis in ancient times.
In "The Scorpion King" movie, Dwayne "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.440
Rock" Johnson — in his first lead role —&nbsp;
takes on the part of the Scorpion King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.360
though in the days before he became the&nbsp;
legendary ruler. Instead, he’s a mercenary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.960
who’s been hired to kill a sorceress&nbsp;
who's conquering tribe after local tribe.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.080
"The Scorpion King" spawned four&nbsp;
direct-to-video sequels in its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.942
right, though it was one&nbsp;
and done for Johnson, alas.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.400
When it comes to "Jumanji," nothing beats&nbsp;
the '90s original, starring Robin Williams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:40.400
The late, great comedic actor took on the&nbsp;
role of the adult version of Alan Parrish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:45.280
a young boy who gets sucked into the game in the&nbsp;
1960s, literally; he's trapped in the world of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.160
the titular magic board game. A couple of decades&nbsp;
later, two kids discover the cursed board game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:55.600
unwittingly releasing Alan from its confines, and&nbsp;
forcing them to finally win the game… or else!

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.680
In addition to the sequel it would later receive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.000
"Jumanji" was spun off into a slightly&nbsp;
more technological direction with 2005's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.600
"Zathura: A Space Adventure." Of course, in&nbsp;
2017, "Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle" served&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.160
as the first direct sequel to the original film&nbsp;
and saw the game change media into a video game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.640
with heavy hitters like Dwayne Johnson, Kevin&nbsp;
Hart, Karen Gillan, and Jack Black as part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:19.280
of the cast — and they all reprised their&nbsp;
roles in 2019's "Jumanji: The Next Level."

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.240
Just like the "Jumanji" franchise, viewers&nbsp;
have options when it comes to the adventures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:29.360
of Lara Croft. The 2001 action adventure film,&nbsp;
"Lara Croft: Tomb Raider," saw actor Angelina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.480
Jolie bring the title character to life in all her&nbsp;
skin-tight glory. Her first outing as the titular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.880
adventurer and star of the "Tomb Raider" video&nbsp;
game franchise sees her up against the Illuminati,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.040
joined by a pre-James Bond Daniel Daniel Craig&nbsp;
as they race to assemble an object that allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:48.000
the person who wields it to control time.&nbsp;
Jolie reprised the role in 2003's "Lara Croft:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.440
Tomb Raider – The Cradle of Life," with&nbsp;
the on-screen sparks this time flying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.760
between her and still-rising star Gerard&nbsp;
Butler as the two seek out Pandora's Box.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:00.720
Jolie declined to take up the role a third time&nbsp;
and "Tomb Raider" rebooted the franchise in 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.520
with actor Alicia Vikander [uh-LISS-ee-uh&nbsp;
vih-KAN-der] taking up the mantle of Lara&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.920
Croft in what amounts to an origin story. The&nbsp;
reboot failed to impress critics, managing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:13.200
middling 52% critics score on Rotten Tomatoes, but&nbsp;
Vikander received praise for her performance and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.040
the movie did well enough at the box office for&nbsp;
a "Tomb Raider" sequel to get the green light.

00:06:18.196 --> 00:06:22.000
"Stardust" springs to life from the brilliant&nbsp;
mind of celebrated writer Neil Gaiman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.800
The 2007 fantasy adventure romp follows&nbsp;
the exploits of Tristan Thorn, a bumbling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:31.120
but romantic young shopkeeper who's so smitten&nbsp;
with local beauty Victoria that he promises to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.600
journey to retrieve a fallen star for her hand&nbsp;
in marriage. And from there, hijinks ensue!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.880
"Stardust" proved popular with both critics and&nbsp;
audiences, earning a certified fresh rating of 77%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.680
from critics, and an even better 86% audience&nbsp;
score. If you like your romance with a side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:49.360
of magical adventure — or vice versa&nbsp;
— then "Stardust" is the film for you!

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.120
Like "Stardust," "The League of&nbsp;
Extraordinary Gentlemen" came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.040
from the mind of a legendary graphic&nbsp;
novel writer, in this case Alan Moore.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.960
"LXG," as the film was marketed, adapts the&nbsp;
graphic novel series of the same name and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:06.080
unites a handful of popular adventure characters&nbsp;
as the titular team. Legendary big game hunter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.320
and adventurer Allan Quartermain - played by&nbsp;
Sean Connery - is recruited out of Africa to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.040
lead a squad featuring the likes of Dorian Grey,&nbsp;
whose immortality is tied to a portrait that ages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:19.360
in his stead; Mina Harker, whose vampirism&nbsp;
is a result of her husband Jonathan's former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:24.240
employment by Count Dracula; the Invisible Man,&nbsp;
Rodney Skinner, a thief who stole the secret to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.920
invisibility from its creator; Nemo, captain of&nbsp;
the submarine Nautilus and maybe a pirate as well;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:35.680
American secret service agent Tom Sawyer; and Dr.&nbsp;
Jekyll and his abominable counterpart, Mr. Hyde.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:40.320
The ambitious adventure film drew characters from&nbsp;
the works of Mark Twain, Oscar Wilde, Jules Verne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.920
Robert Louis Stevenson, Bram Stoker, H.G. Wells,&nbsp;
and more, just like its comic book inspiration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:51.200
It fared well at the box office — grossing&nbsp;
$179 million against a $78 million budget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.720
though critics weren't as kind to&nbsp;
the edgy steampunk romp as audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.640
as the film earned just a 17%&nbsp;
critics rating on Rotten tomatoes.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:02.320
But hey, if you like your dumb fun extra&nbsp;
dumb, this should be right up your alley!

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:07.360
Action, adventure, and forces beyond what&nbsp;
mere mortals can reckon await viewers in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:10.240
the "Pirates of the Caribbean"&nbsp;
franchise, unquestionably the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.920
most successful cinematic adaptation of&nbsp;
a theme park ride that has ever existed.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:18.000
The swashbuckling adventure series follows&nbsp;
the misadventures of Captain Jack Sparrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.920
who's simply trying to get his ship back&nbsp;
in the first film. In the course of events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.240
his path crosses with that of pirate-obsessed&nbsp;
socialite Elizabeth Swan, and Will Turner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.000
the blacksmith who's in love with her — so&nbsp;
much so that he'll break Jack out of prison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.160
if he agrees to help rescue her from her pirate&nbsp;
captors. Who just so happen to be the mutinous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:38.960
crew that marooned Jack, stealing his ship in&nbsp;
the first place. It's like it was meant to be!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:43.200
The 2003 film "Pirates of the Caribbean: The&nbsp;
Curse of the Black Pearl" spawned a trilogy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:48.560
that included "Dead Man's Chest" in 2006&nbsp;
and "At World's End" in 2007. Stars Johnny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.680
Depp and Geoffrey Rush both returned&nbsp;
for the fourth and fifth installments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.960
"On Stranger Tides" in 2011 and "Dead&nbsp;
Men Tell No Tales" in 2017. Together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:01.280
the films have grossed more than $4.5&nbsp;
billion worldwide and a sixth "Pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:04.480
of the Caribbean" movie will reboot the&nbsp;
franchise without Depp at the wheel.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:05.840
"You cheated!"

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:07.840
"Pirate!"

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:11.120
Adventure lovers who haven't seen&nbsp;
the cult classic "The Princess Bride"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:14.160
would do well to resolve that&nbsp;
issue as quickly as possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.080
It packs in plenty of heart and wit,&nbsp;
in addition to danger and excitement.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.120
Adapted from the novel of the same&nbsp;
name, "The Princess Bride" follows the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.600
travails of Westley , a young stableboy who&nbsp;
serves Princess Buttercup without question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.080
with the two eventually falling in love. Westley&nbsp;
sets out to make something of himself in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:34.720
be worthy of Buttercup's hand in marriage but is&nbsp;
waylaid by the Dread Pirate Roberts, well known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:40.080
for taking no prisoners. Heartbroken, Buttercup&nbsp;
is engaged to Prince Humperdinck against her will.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:44.880
Thankfully — yes, thankfully — she is kidnapped&nbsp;
before her wedding by three scallywags,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.280
a thief named Vizzini, a giant named&nbsp;
Fezzik, and a swordsman named Inigo Montoya,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.280
who seeks to avenge his father's death and&nbsp;
spawn a million memes. They're pursued by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.800
Prince Humperdinck and his soldiers, in&nbsp;
addition to a mysterious man in black.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:02.160
The 1987 film is an enduring favorite among movie&nbsp;
lovers of multiple generations. While it didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.120
smash any box office records — it grossed&nbsp;
$31 million globally against its $15 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.160
budget — it was a modest financial success.&nbsp;
But it's gone on to become a cult classic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.440
So you want to watch the most fun&nbsp;
adventure movie of all time? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.212
"Princess Bride" has just&nbsp;
one answer to that request:

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.735
"As you wish!"

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:26.320
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:29.600
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite movies are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.380
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

